y space that fits the time before your next commitment.","short_summary":"Nold gives students a named campus destination for exercise and recreation between obligations.","evidence_claim":"The current advising handbook lists Nold Hall's equipped gym, exercise room, lockers, and showers; Campus Recreation documents fitness, group exercise, and intramural programs.","source_url":"https://www.farmingdale.edu/aaic/aaic-handbook.shtml","source_title":"Academic Advisement Handbook","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://map.farmingdale.edu/","access_notes":"Access may require a valid Farmingdale ID and depends on current recreation schedules, team use, classes, and event closures.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"fsc-giving-garden","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Giving Garden","title":"Join a Scheduled Giving Garden Work Session","subtitle":"Twelve growing beds supporting the FSC Food Pantry","notes":"Email the Sustainability Manager to arrange a volunteer shift, then follow the garden's maintenance plan instead of tending or harvesting independently.","short_summary":"The garden turns scheduled student and community work into produce for the campus pantry.","evidence_claim":"FSC says the Giving Garden has 12 beds, donates most of its produce to the FSC Food Pantry, and offers scheduled or regular volunteer opportunities.","source_url":"https://www.farmingdale.edu/sustainability/giving-garden.shtml","source_title":"Giving Garden","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":"https://map.farmingdale.edu/","access_notes":"Volunteer participation must be arranged with the campus Sustainability Manager; consult the campus map's sustainability layer for the garden location.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnin